type? xor~ (make vector! [integer! 8 [12 10 6]]) (make vector! [integer! 8 [10 12 6]])| #(vector!)

=== neither operand is changed ===
the bitset on the left, afterwards          | #(bitset! #{00000000000000000000000060})
the bitset on the right, afterwards         | #(bitset! #{00000000000000000000000030})
the vector on the left, afterwards          | #(int8! [12 10 6])
the vector on the right, afterwards         | #(int8! [10 12 6])
the tuple on the left, afterwards           | 12.10.6
the binary on the left, afterwards          | #{0F10}
the binary on the right, afterwards         | #{33}
the typeset on the left, afterwards         | make typeset! [string! file! email! ref! url! tag!]
the typeset on the right, afterwards        | make typeset! [block! paren! path! set-path! get-path! lit-path! hash!]
the pair on the left, afterwards            | 12x10

=== degenerate operands are ordinary operands ===
and~ #{} #{0F10}                            | #{0000}
and~ #{0F10} #{}                            | #{0000}
and~ #{} #{}                                | #{}
and~ (make bitset! #{}) (charset "ab")      | #(bitset! #{})
and~ (charset "ab") (make bitset! #{})      | #(bitset! #{})
and~ (make typeset! []) any-string!         | make typeset! []
and~ any-string! (make typeset! [])         | make typeset! []
and~ (make vector! [integer! 8 []]) 10      | #(int8! [])
and~ 0 0                                    | 0
and~ 0x0 0                                  | 0x0
and~ 0.0.0 0                                | 0.0.0
and~ 0.0.0 0.0.0                            | 0.0.0
and~ -1 -1                                  | -1
or~ -1 0                                    | -1
xor~ -1 -1                                  | 0
and~ 0 12                                   | 0
and~ 12 0                                   | 0
and~ (to char! 0) (to char! 0)              | #"^@"
and~ false false                            | #(false)
or~ false false                             | #(false)

=== every spelling reaches the same code ===
and~ 12 10                                  | 8
12 and 10                                   | 8
12 & 10                                     | 8
or~ 12 10                                   | 14
12 or 10                                    | 14
12 | 10                                     | 14
xor~ 12 10                                  | 6
12 xor 10                                   | 6
and~ 12x10 10x12                            | 8x8
12x10 and 10x12                             | 8x8
12x10 & 10x12                               | 8x8
or~ 12x10 10x12                             | 14x14
12x10 or 10x12                              | 14x14
12x10 | 10x12                               | 14x14
xor~ 12x10 10x12                            | 6x6
12x10 xor 10x12                             | 6x6
and~ 12 10x12                               | !not-related
12 and 10x12                                | !not-related
12 & 10x12                                  | !not-related
